ml, go.mod, Makefile), and no .github/ or CI config, confirmed by directory listing; therefore no repository lint/typecheck/build/test gate was bypassed. Permissive-input and unenumerated-error classes do not apply to a static file deliverable. No scope shrinkage: the objective has exactly one deliverable and it is present.\n\nE2E and video evidence: no QA E2E video is referenced in the ledger, receipt, or run artifacts, and none is required — the deliverable is a file, not a user-visible UI or CLI surface, and there is no runnable application to drive with playwright-cli or tmux. Byte-level inspection of both the worktree file and the committed git blob is the strongest available end-to-end proof and I reproduced it myself. A sibling additionally grepped the run directory for media files and found none, so there is no unverified E2E claim to police.\n\nBaseline caveat (non-blocking): the review contract names `origin/main` as baseline, but `git remote -v` is empty and `git diff origin/main` fails with \"fatal: ambiguous argument origin/main: unknown revision\". I used the repository's only ancestor commit 4a791f1 (init) as baseline, which fully covers the delta since the branch has just two commits. Both siblings hit and reported the same environment fact independently.\n\nCoordination: I ran one bounded evidence-exchange round. I sent my preliminary PASS verdict and command evidence, and received preliminary verdicts from the Completion Reviewer and the Evidence Reviewer, both PASS with matching byte-level evidence. Both raised the same interpretation challenge — LF-terminated 32-byte line versus a 31-byte no-newline form — and I answered that the POSIX line reading is correct and that `git diff` shows no \"\\ No newline at end of file\"; the visible characters match character-for-character under either reading, so it cannot move the verdict. The Evidence Reviewer flagged a stale \"32-character text\" phrasing inside the worker subagent artifact; that count phrasing does not appear in the ledger objective and the delivered bytes are correct, so it is narration in a non-deliverable artifact, not a contract defect, and I raise no finding for it. Deliberation did not change my verdict; I return my own decision.",
